  "best_competitor_by_endpoint_metric_csv": "<WORKSPACE>\\extensions\\best_competitor_by_endpoint_metric.csv",
  "review_facing_prose": [
    "The four capture-order windows now compare three newly fitted hierarchy maps against the same existing fresh flat component. Family/local LGBM components use 380 trees and the frozen base rows; flat XGB 520, flat LGBM 380 and utility-calibrated meta-models were reused, not retrained. Each hierarchy blend uses fixed equal weights. No gate was fitted for these capture controls.",
    "Across all four dependent capture windows, taxonomy blend macro_f1 averaged 0.621426 versus 0.620067 for temperature_flat_blend; taxonomy minus control was 0.001360. These are descriptive means from one fitted seed, not independent-replicate inference.",
    "Across all four dependent capture windows, taxonomy blend rare_recall averaged 0.548859 versus 0.552048 for temperature_flat_blend; taxonomy minus control was -0.003189. These are descriptive means from one fitted seed, not independent-replicate inference.",
    "Across all four dependent capture windows, taxonomy blend macro_f1 averaged 0.621426 versus 0.638285 for newton_flat_stacker; taxonomy minus control was -0.016859. These are descriptive means from one fitted seed, not independent-replicate inference.",
    "Across all four dependent capture windows, taxonomy blend rare_recall averaged 0.548859 versus 0.519084 for newton_flat_stacker; taxonomy minus control was 0.029775. These are descriptive means from one fitted seed, not independent-replicate inference.",
    "For the same shared-flat comparison against cyclic_blend, mean taxonomy-minus-control macro_f1 was -0.002228; taxonomy was higher in 0/4 dependent windows and lower in 4/4. These descriptive directions do not establish population significance or universal taxonomy superiority.",
    "For the same shared-flat comparison against cyclic_blend, mean taxonomy-minus-control rare_recall was 0.002121; taxonomy was higher in 4/4 dependent windows and lower in 0/4. These descriptive directions do not establish population significance or universal taxonomy superiority.",
    "For the same shared-flat comparison against support_matched_blend, mean taxonomy-minus-control macro_f1 was -0.000503; taxonomy was higher in 2/4 dependent windows and lower in 2/4. These descriptive directions do not establish population significance or universal taxonomy superiority.",
    "For the same shared-flat comparison against support_matched_blend, mean taxonomy-minus-control rare_recall was 0.002369; taxonomy was higher in 2/4 dependent windows and lower in 2/4. These descriptive directions do not establish population significance or universal taxonomy superiority.",
    "All nine Table 4 arms, including the taxonomy, cyclic and support gates, retain the original canonical-v10 six-split ECE10 results. Capture cyclic/support arms are separate fixed blends, not those gates. Capture file order is a proxy, not timestamp validation; no physical edge hardware was available."
  ],
  "all_nine_arms_retrained": false,
  "method_scope_change": "The ninth formal capture arm is newly available real_taxonomy, replacing the audit-only legacy_flat_xgb; the other five fresh flat and three blend IDs remain. Cyclic/support standalone hierarchies are additional audit arms.",
